function help(){modalKind='help';dialog(`<div class="overline">3D SURVIVAL FIELD GUIDE</div><h2>Explore the Frontier</h2><p><b>WASD / arrow keys</b> move. <b>G</b> toggles optional phone motion controls (permission requested only when you enable it). <b>WILDLIFE</b> opens a research journal; scanning wildlife records species and earns salvage. Build a wildlife habitat to attract animals. Credits for the optional rigged scout model are in the field guide. <b>Shift</b> sprints. Drag across the world to orbit the camera; scroll to change height. <b>V</b> switches first/third person. <b>E</b> gathers nearby supplies and activates landmarks. <b>Space</b> scans once crafted; <b>J</b> opens the journal and <b>M</b> toggles the field map. Change graphics between HQ and ECO in the HUD.</p><p>Build structures using the Craft panel and click the ground near your explorer. Fuel generators with wood. Powered extractors automatically generate stone and scrap. Your settlement persists when you return from expeditions.</p><p><b>Rigged avatar:</b> The pre-rigged CesiumMan sample character (CC BY 4.0, © Cesium) loads from Arcadia's locally hosted asset when available; standalone files may fetch the asset from GitHub. See Wildlife Field Guide for the license link. The built-in explorer is used offline. <b>Saving:</b> Each of your three free worlds stays in this browser. Export a backup from the Journal and restore it on the world-selection screen. Save data is not shared with Roblox or other devices.</p><footer><button class="btn accent" data-action="close">Start playing</button></footer>`)}
